{
 "about": "Scanned CC0 textures from ambientCG (ambientcg.com, CC0: free for any use). Tools/fetch_textures.py downloads them here (the images aren't in git); Tools/ue_build_level.py builds the land and road materials from the roles. 'tile_m' is how many metres one repeat covers. The stone roles are for the walls, scars, boulders and barns (Tools/buttertubs_stone.py): 'stone' lichened limestone, 'stone_bare' bare bedded limestone, 'moss' for the moss on them. A role's optional 'ue' block names textures already in the project (Megascans from Fab, which aren't in git); the CC0 'id' is the fallback when they're missing. 'masonry' is the rubble walling of the houses and barns. The rider_ roles are the riding kit (Tools/ue_build_level.py rider_materials): 'mean' is the scan's linear mean colour and 'rough_mean' its mean roughness, so the kit can be tinted and scaled to the finishes in Data/Rider/rider.json; recompute them if a role's id changes. 'bark' is the trees' bark (M_Tree, on the models' UV1; tile_m must match BARK_M in Tools/tree_models.py; 'mean' is its average linear brightness, which M_Tree divides out so the trees keep their own bark colours). The shed_ roles are the shed's surfaces (Tools/ue_build_shed.py scanned): each is tinted so its 'mean' comes out as Torque Shed's colour for that surface, and its roughness scaled from 'rough_mean' to Torque Shed's; a Megascans 'ue' block, when the PC has one from Fab, is used first.",
